                <pb facs="0158" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v41/pg112"/>

                <head>38. Memorandum From the Assistant Secretary of State-Designate for European
                    and Eurasian Affairs (Eagleburger) to Secretary of State-Designate Haig<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d38-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1981-01-01">January 1, 1981</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following more or less random thoughts on some of the procedural and
                    substantive problems you will face as Secretary of State are drawn from over 20
                    years experience with the fudge factory, 2 transitions, and almost four years as
                    an Ambassador to a middle-sized post. As you will note, I list more problems
                    than answers.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here are discussions not related to human rights.]</p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Human Rights</p>
                <p>I spent 3½ years keeping Pat Derian out of Belgrade, so my prejudices are clear.
                    But with all of that, a nuanced human rights policy that is kept in perspective
                    is a major weapon against the Soviets, a sometime effective tool with erstwhile
                    friends, and a bow in the direction of the left in this country.</p>
                <p>The Carter Administration handled the issue badly, but you ought not throw the
                    baby out with the bath water.</p>
                <p>One warning: if you turn human rights questions over totally to the bureaus, you
                    will soon find that they will be handled with even less consistency than in the
                    recent past.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here are discussions not related to human rights.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
